* text=auto eol=lf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Binary files. The `* text=auto` rule above asks git to *guess* whether a file is text, and
# the guess is only "no NUL byte in the first 8000 bytes". A jar that guesses wrong is checked
# out with CRLF injected into it, and Java then reports it as a missing main class rather than
# as a corrupt archive - which is a long way from the truth. Declare, do not guess.
*.jar   binary
*.zip   binary
*.gz    binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.gif   binary
*.ico   binary
*.pdf   binary
*.xlsx  binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf   binary
